    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d820">

                <pb facs="0942" n="930" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg930"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">703.5492/18: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-04-15">April 15, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>948. Your 1420, 9th.<anchor n="47" xml:id="d820-f1"/> Inform Thai Government that
                    limitation of written and oral communication between Swiss representative and
                    American Legation Bangkok and refusal by Thai-Japanese mixed committee of
                    permission for American official group to retain sufficient domestic servants
                    necessary under prevailing climatic conditions for adequate maintenance of
                    health do not correspond to favorable treatment accorded Japanese officials in
                    United States (Thai officials are of course completely at liberty) and that this
                    Government expects the removal of these inequalities in treatment of American
                    officials in Thailand.</p>
                <p>Japanese Government should be informed of foregoing with statement this
                    Government wishes instructions to be issued to Japanese officials in Thailand to
                    work for desired improvement in situation of American officials there.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
